{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788119711663,"sessionID":"ses_fabcc0d67ffe81ceFkgf1oLPKJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8fb5c086379c4c19","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs","newString":"#[derive(Default)]\nstruct Helpers {\n    select: bool,\n    field: bool,\n    index: bool,\n    unwrap: bool,\n    arith: bool,\n    arith64: bool,\n    collect: bool,\n    jsonlines: bool,\n    tail: bool,\n    str_cmp: bool,\n    chars: bool,\n    sum: bool,\n    sum64: bool,\n    max: bool,\n    eq: bool,\n}","oldString":"#[derive(Default)]\nstruct Helpers {\n    select: bool,\n    field: bool,\n    index: bool,\n    unwrap: bool,\n    arith: bool,\n    arith64: bool,\n    collect: bool,\n    jsonlines: bool,\n    tail: bool,\n    str_cmp: bool,\n    chars: bool,\n    eq: bool,\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n@@ -431,8 +431,11 @@\n     jsonlines: bool,\n     tail: bool,\n     str_cmp: bool,\n     chars: bool,\n+    sum: bool,\n+    sum64: bool,\n+    max: bool,\n     eq: bool,\n }\n \n /// Which helper a comparison reaches for, decided by the operator and the operand type rather\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n@@ -431,8 +431,11 @@\n     jsonlines: bool,\n     tail: bool,\n     str_cmp: bool,\n     chars: bool,\n+    sum: bool,\n+    sum64: bool,\n+    max: bool,\n     eq: bool,\n }\n \n /// Which helper a comparison reaches for, decided by the operator and the operand type rather\n","additions":3,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/emit_js.rs","time":{"start":1788119711658,"end":1788119711660}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me edit the JS Helpers struct, add helpers, walk, emit table, and match arms.\n\nJS: Int is Number with `|0` narrowing; Int64 is BigInt. So sum over Int should narrow per-step with `|0`. Since mixing Number and BigInt in `+` throws, the sum helper must be written to handle each element type uniformly. If the elements are all Number (Int) or all BigInt (Int64), the accumulator is same type. For Int: `acc = (acc + v[i]) | 0`. For Int64: `acc = acc + v[i]` (BigInt wraps automatically? BigInt is arbitrary precision! `BigInt` does NOT wrap at 64 bits. The existing arith64 wraps via `BigInt.asIntN(64, ...)`. So Int64 sum needs `BigInt.asIntN(64, acc + v[i])`.\n\nSo the sum helper needs to know the width. Let me pass a flag or emit different helper calls. Since JS arithmetic needs `|0` for Int and `BigInt.asIntN(64, ...)` for Int64, I'll write one helper that takes the accumulator and element (they're consistent types) and a `narrow` boolean:\n\nActually simpler: two helper variants or one helper with a function argument. Hmm. Let me think.\n\nOption: `tl_sum(v)` assumes Number elements and narrows with `|0`. And `tl_sum64(v)` for BigInt. That's two helpers. The emit branches on elem type. That's clean and mirrors arith/arith64 split.\n\n```js\nfunction tl_sum(v) {\n  let acc = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < v.length; i++) acc = (acc + v[i]) | 0;\n  return acc;\n}\nfunction tl_sum64(v) {\n  let acc = 0n;\n  for (let i = 0; i < v.length; i++) acc = BigInt.asIntN(64, acc + v[i]);\n  return acc;\n}\n```\n\nFor max:\n```js\nfunction tl_max(v) {\n  if (v.length === 0) return \"none\";\n  let m = v[0];\n  for (let i = 1; i < v.length; i++) if (v[i] > m) m = v[i];\n  return { some: m };\n}\n```\n\nJS `>` works for both Number and BigInt. Good, one helper.\n\nNow the walk: I need `used.sum` and `used.sum64`. And emit: `Builtin::Sum => if elem == Int { tl_sum(...) } else { tl_sum64(...) }`. And `Builtin::Max => tl_max(...)`.\n\nLet me add fields: `sum: bool, sum64: bool, max: bool`.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0543d7976001E0gYGbQUsmgY85","sessionID":"ses_fabcc0d67ffe81ceFkgf1oLPKJ","messageID":"msg_0543d523e001uIgtojZge4rDK1"}}
