{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788119749732,"sessionID":"ses_fabcc0d67ffe81ceFkgf1oLPKJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-99199cb3e9ae33ad","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs","newString":"            // `.reverse()` mutates in place, so the spread copy is what keeps this an ordinary\n            // expression rather than a statement with a visible side effect on `arg`.\n            Builtin::Reverse => format!(\"[...{}].reverse()\", expr(enums, arg)),\n            // One fold per width, since the element type picks the runtime integer type.\n            Builtin::Sum => {\n                if tir::runtime_elem(&arg.ty) == Some(&Type::Int) {\n                    format!(\"tl_sum({})\", expr(enums, arg))\n                } else {\n                    format!(\"tl_sum64({})\", expr(enums, arg))\n                }\n            }\n            Builtin::Max => format!(\"tl_max({})\", expr(enums, arg)),","oldString":"            // `.reverse()` mutates in place, so the spread copy is what keeps this an ordinary\n            // expression rather than a statement with a visible side effect on `arg`.\n            Builtin::Reverse => format!(\"[...{}].reverse()\", expr(enums, arg)),"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n@@ -728,8 +728,17 @@\n }\n // `.reverse()` mutates in place, so the spread copy is what keeps this an ordinary\n // expression rather than a statement with a visible side effect on `arg`.\n Builtin::Reverse => format!(\"[...{}].reverse()\", expr(enums, arg)),\n+// One fold per width, since the element type picks the runtime integer type.\n+Builtin::Sum => {\n+    if tir::runtime_elem(&arg.ty) == Some(&Type::Int) {\n+        format!(\"tl_sum({})\", expr(enums, arg))\n+    } else {\n+        format!(\"tl_sum64({})\", expr(enums, arg))\n+    }\n+}\n+Builtin::Max => format!(\"tl_max({})\", expr(enums, arg)),\n // The names come from the checked type, not the object value, so `arg` is evaluated\n // only for whatever else it does (a division inside it must still throw) and its\n // value discarded with the comma operator.\n Builtin::Fields => {\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-140/src/emit_js.rs\n@@ -728,8 +728,17 @@\n }\n // `.reverse()` mutates in place, so the spread copy is what keeps this an ordinary\n // expression rather than a statement with a visible side effect on `arg`.\n Builtin::Reverse => format!(\"[...{}].reverse()\", expr(enums, arg)),\n+// One fold per width, since the element type picks the runtime integer type.\n+Builtin::Sum => {\n+    if tir::runtime_elem(&arg.ty) == Some(&Type::Int) {\n+        format!(\"tl_sum({})\", expr(enums, arg))\n+    } else {\n+        format!(\"tl_sum64({})\", expr(enums, arg))\n+    }\n+}\n+Builtin::Max => format!(\"tl_max({})\", expr(enums, arg)),\n // The names come from the checked type, not the object value, so `arg` is evaluated\n // only for whatever else it does (a division inside it must still throw) and its\n // value discarded with the comma operator.\n Builtin::Fields => {\n","additions":9,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/emit_js.rs","time":{"start":1788119749728,"end":1788119749730}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_0543de3ce001BVtj4R7YUPSwZq","sessionID":"ses_fabcc0d67ffe81ceFk